### Client Ticket Tracker: API requests
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, Rider, and Visual Studio 2022+.
# REST Client keeps the auth cookie between requests automatically, so run
# "Login" first, then anything else. (docs/LOCAL-SETUP.md has curl versions.)

@api = http://localhost:5080/api
@email = agent@example.com
@password = change-this-password
# Sample data creates tickets 1-10, so the first ticket you create is usually 11.
# If "Create a ticket" returns a different id, change this.
@ticketId = 11

### Health (no login needed)
GET {{api}}/health

### Login: sets the ctt.auth cookie
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Who am I?
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Queue: all tickets, most urgent first
GET {{api}}/tickets

### Queue: open tickets only
GET {{api}}/tickets?status=Open

### Queue: escalated + urgent
GET {{api}}/tickets?status=Escalated&priority=Urgent

### Ticket detail
GET {{api}}/tickets/1

### Create a ticket
POST {{api}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "CSV import rejects dates in DD/MM/YYYY",
  "description": "Client's import file uses UK date format and every row fails validation.",
  "category": "Bug",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "clientName": "Harbor Freight Lines",
  "clientEmail": "support@harborfreight.example"
}

### Invalid: 400 with one error per field (title/description too short, priority missing, bad email)
POST {{api}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Hi", "description": "Short.", "category": "Bug", "clientName": "X", "clientEmail": "nope" }

### Invalid enum value: 400 from the JSON reader itself ("Feature" isn't a TicketCategory)
# The body can't be deserialised at all, so this one reports only the JSON error.
POST {{api}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Valid title", "description": "A long enough description.", "category": "Feature", "priority": "Low", "clientName": "Test Co", "clientEmail": "t@test.example" }

### Start work on the new ticket (Open -> InProgress)
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "InProgress" }

### Escalate WITHOUT a note -> 400
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Escalated" }

### Escalate with a note -> 200, and a warning line in the API console
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Escalated", "note": "Reproduced on staging; SSO callback returns 504 after 30s." }

### Resolve
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Resolved", "resolutionNotes": "Engineering raised the SSO callback timeout; verified with client." }

### Illegal transition: Resolved -> Escalated -> 400
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Escalated", "note": "should fail" }

### Add an internal comment
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Client confirmed the fix on their side." }

### Search by ID
GET {{api}}/tickets/search?q=%232

### Search by client-name prefix (matches both Acme clients)
GET {{api}}/tickets/search?q=acme

### Search by keywords in different fields (title has "login", description has "timeout")
GET {{api}}/tickets/search?q=login%20timeout

### Wildcard escaping: searching for a literal "%" (URL-encoded as %25).
# Unescaped, LIKE '%%' would match EVERY client name and return all tickets.
# Escaped, it only finds the ticket whose title contains a "%" character.
GET {{api}}/tickets/search?q=%25

### Logout
POST {{api}}/auth/logout

### Triage: is the optional LLM suggestion feature configured?
GET {{api}}/triage/status

### Triage: suggest a category and priority (404 if Triage:ApiKey isn't set)
POST {{api}}/triage/suggest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Password reset email never arrives", "description": "Members say reset emails never arrive. Checked spam. Everyone affected since this morning." }
